    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0279" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8993: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-27T13:00:00-04:00">July 27, 1937—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>320. Your 505, July 27, 1 p.m. Department is telegraphing Peiping and
                        Tokyo<anchor n="86" xml:id="d277-f1"/> instructing our Embassies there to
                    confer immediately with the British Embassies and in their discretion to take
                    action on lines parallel with the British action toward dissuading the Japanese
                    authorities from proceeding with any plan for military operations which would be
                    likely to endanger the lives of American nationals.</p>
                <p>Please inform the Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
